Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:03:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] =?UTF-8?q?hw/input:=20gt911=20=E2=80=94=20a=20relea?=
 =?UTF-8?q?se=20IS=20a=20report=20(status=200x80,=20not=20not-ready)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

fill_report returned an all-zero status byte when no touch was pending,
i.e. 'buffer not ready' — the driver then retried for 20ms, timed out
with -ETIME and never reported anything, so TouchEnd never reached
userspace: the pressed button stayed down and the occupied slot killed
all further interaction. A real GT911 reports buffer-ready with ZERO
contacts on release; do the same (0x80) so the driver's zero-contact
path emits the proper release.
---
 hw/input/gt911.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/input/gt911.c b/hw/input/gt911.c
index dedbd13..a301c00 100644
--- a/hw/input/gt911.c
+++ b/hw/input/gt911.c
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 static void gt911_fill_report(GT911State *s, uint8_t *buf, int len)
 {
     memset(buf, 0, len);
+    buf[0] = 0x80;                      /* buffer-ready + 0 contacts: a
+                                        * release IS a report — with 0x00
+                                        * the driver retries for 20ms and
+                                        * gives up without ever sending
+                                        * TouchEnd, leaving the button
+                                        * stuck down */
     if (s->pending) {
         buf[0] = 0x81;                  /* ready + 1 contact */
         buf[1] = 0x00;                  /* track 0 */
